{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), the dominant uncertainty is whether the image modality carries any useful signal at all. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) establishes the image-modality baseline under the same simple singleprofile setting, enabling a clean modality comparison against config_001. This is the highest-information next step: if image-only performs comparably or better than RNA-only, multimodal fusion (configs 016+) becomes a promising direction worth investing in; if image-only is weak, we can deprioritize multimodal and image-encoder variants and focus budget on RNA encoder and multiprofile improvements. Testing this before any multimodal or multiprofile variant avoids committing budget to complex combinations whose value depends on the untested premise that both modalities contribute signal."
}

